==English==

===Etymology===
From the name of Roman emperors, {{etyl|la}} ''[[constans]]'' - ''[[constantis]]'', constant, steadfast.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{given name|male|from=Latin}}.

====Quotations====
* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 6-1|I}}:Scene 2:
*: Helen, the mother of great '''Constantine''' / Nor yet Saint Philip's daughters were like thee.

